.TH RKB 1 "2026-05-17" "rkb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rkb \- repository-level kanban board for AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rkb build
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B rkb plan
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBrkb\fR manages a kanban board stored in \fI.kanban-board\fR at the
repository root. It is designed for AI agents to break complex tasks
into tickets and track their progress.
.PP
The \fBbuild\fR subcommands mutate the board file. The \fBplan\fR
subcommands are read-only and output JSON to stdout.
.SH BUILD COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the board file if it does not exist. If it already exists it is
validated rather than overwritten: an existing board that cannot be read
is reported and the command exits non-zero.
.TP
.B add \-\-title \fIstr\fR [options]
Add a new ticket to the backlog. Options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-description \fIstr\fR
Full description or acceptance criteria.
.TP
.B \-\-priority \fIn\fR
Priority level (1\(en5). Enforced: a value outside 1\(en5, or one
that is not a number, is rejected and no ticket is created.
.TP
.B \-\-assignee \fIstr\fR
Name of the assigned agent.
.TP
.B \-\-tags \fIa,b,c\fR
Comma-separated list of tags.
.TP
.B \-\-blocked-by \fI1,2\fR
Comma-separated ticket IDs this ticket depends on. Each ID must be a
positive number; a token that is not is rejected and nothing is
written, rather than being skipped. Ids that do not exist yet are
accepted, since dependencies may point forward.
.RE
.PP
The assigned id comes from \fBnext_id\fR, which increases monotonically
and is never reused. \fBrkb build rm\fR does not decrement it, so ids
have gaps once tickets are deleted; that is expected and not a sign of
lost data. Ids must stay stable because surviving tickets hold
\fBblocked_by\fR references to them.
.TP
.B move \fIid\fR \fIstatus\fR
Change a ticket\(cqs status. Warns if blocked tickets are not done.
.TP
.B edit \fIid\fR \fIfield\fR \fIvalue\fR
Append to a ticket field without discarding what is already there.
Appends a new line to \fBdescription\fR, and adds only missing elements to
\fBtags\fR and \fBblocked_by\fR. An append that adds nothing prints
"ok (no change)" and still exits 0.
.RS
.PP
\fBtitle\fR, \fBassignee\fR and \fBpriority\fR hold a single value, so
\fBedit\fR refuses them. Use
.B overwrite
for those. To clear any field, use
.BI overwrite " " id " " field " \(dq\(dq"
.RE
.TP
.B overwrite \fIid\fR \fIfield\fR \fIvalue\fR
Replace a ticket field\(cqs value outright. Pass an empty value,
.BR \(dq\(dq ,
to clear it. Every field
.B edit
accepts is accepted here too, and this is the only way to clear one.
.TP
.B rm \fIid\fR
Remove a ticket from the board.
.TP
.B archive-done
Move all tickets with status \fBdone\fR to \fBarchive\fR.
.SH PLAN COMMANDS
.TP
.B list [\-\-pretty]
List all tickets as JSON (or as a table with \-\-pretty).
.TP
.B show \fIid\fR [\-\-pretty]
Show a single ticket as JSON.
.TP
.B stats [\-\-pretty]
Show ticket counts per column, blocked count, and unassigned count.
.TP
.B lint [\-\-json]
Check the board for problems and report them. Read\-only: the board is
never modified. Exits 1 when issues are found.
.TP
.B export
Dump the raw board file to stdout.
.SH COLUMNS
backlog, ready, in-progress, QA, done, archive
.SH BOARD LINT
.B rkb plan lint
checks the board for problems that no other command reports, because every
read path looks up fields by name and so cannot see a field it does not
know. It reports unknown and duplicate ticket keys, missing required
fields, wrong field types, a status that is not a board column, duplicate
ticket ids, dependencies on tickets that do not exist, and board-level
problems such as a missing
.B next_id
or a column list that does not match this build.
.PP
Lint never modifies the board. To repair one, dump it with
.B rkb plan export
and edit the JSON directly; which of two contradictory values should win
is not something a tool should guess.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Usage error or bad argument (missing --title, invalid status), or
.BR "plan lint"
found issues.
.TP
2
Board file error (not found, invalid JSON, I/O failure).
.TP
3
Ticket id not found.
.SH CONCURRENCY
Saves are atomic: the board is written to a uniquely named temporary
file, fsync'd, then renamed over the board, so a reader never sees a
half-written file and an interrupted save cannot corrupt it.
.PP
Locking is
.B not
provided. Two
.B build
commands mutating the same board at the same time is unsupported: both
read the board before either writes, the last rename wins, and the
ticket from the slower process is lost even though it printed
.BR ok .
Run one
.B rkb
command at a time per repository.
.SH FILES
.I .kanban-board
JSON file in the repository root. Add to .gitignore.
.SH AUTHOR
Adam McKenney
